  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Differentiate ${e}^{x}cos\u2061x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=cos\u2061x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}cos\u2061x)^{\u2032} & ={u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{\u2032}\\cdot cos\u2061x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (cos\u2061x)^{\u2032} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(cos\u2061x)+({e}^{x})(-sin\u2061x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}cos\u2061x-{e}^{x}sin\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
